It's common for folks to use wizard mode or explore mode
to solve puzzles.  If you want to do that in your current
game and you save before going into explore mode, then
quit no matter how your experiment turns out and you
restore your saved game, is that still savescumming in
your opinion?

There are times I want to try stuff out with the full
context of my current game.  Try two different approaches
for dealing with the mines end I just arrived at
perhaps.  So I've been known to back up a level, save
the game, then try the two approaches to see how they
work out, and then restore to the original and proceed
based on the outcome of my experiment.  The "real
game" timeline never proceeds the same as either
"experiment game" timelines of course, but I try to
learn some sort of lesson and apply it from then on.

Do folks count that as savescumming?  I know that
saving once you enter mines end and restoring if you
die is definitely savescumming, but what about this
sort of alternate-world scenario sequence?



